\end_inset
 and an experimental value of 
\begin_inset Formula $5.2\,\text{kV/cm}$
\end_inset
. This is a quantitative check of Figure 5(b) that does not depend on reading the 3-D drawing.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Tip field.
\series default
 The space charge suppresses the field at the tip from 
\begin_inset Formula $149.4$
\end_inset
 to 
\begin_inset Formula $-3.6\,\text{kV/cm}$
\end_inset
 at inception. It then recovers quickly, because the applied field grows with 
\begin_inset Formula $V(t)$
\end_inset
 and the drift weakens both the direct and the rod image field at the tip.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Second streamer.
